{
  "node_type": "statement",
  "body": {
    "id": "thm:universal-airy-law",
    "kind": "theorem",
    "statement": "Theorem 1. For every fixed \\(K\\ge2\\) and every zero-sum, \\(\\ell^1\\)-normalized contrast \\(c\\in\\mathcal C_K\\),\n\\[\nR_n(c)=n^{-1}-C_AV_c(s_c/2)^{2/3}n^{-4/3}+o(n^{-4/3}),\n\\qquad\n\\lim_{n\\to\\infty}n^{4/3}d_n(c)=\\Lambda_c.\n\\]\nThe independent allocation \\(q_a^\\star=|c_a|/2\\) on active arms and the total full-label nonlinear Airy estimator \\(\\delta_n^\\star\\) attain the expansion.  If \\(|S_c|=2\\), the reduction proposition gives \\(V_c(s_c/2)=1\\), allows any number of inactive labels, and recovers the published two-arm law.  The new response-alphabet and all-allocation-face argument supplies the closure for \\(|S_c|\\ge3\\).",
    "free_symbols": [
      "K",
      "c",
      "\\mathcal C_K",
      "R_n(c)",
      "n",
      "C_A",
      "V_c",
      "s_c",
      "d_n(c)",
      "\\Lambda_c",
      "q^\\star",
      "\\delta_n^\\star"
    ],
    "depends_on": [
      "def:contrast-class",
      "def:risk-game",
      "def:response-gauge",
      "def:airy-constant",
      "thm:universal-upper",
      "thm:universal-lower",
      "prop:two-arm-reduction"
    ],
    "proof_tex": "Fix \\(K\\ge2\\) and \\(c\\in\\mathcal C_K\\).  By \\(\\mathrm{thm:universal\\text{-}upper}\\),\n\\[\n\\liminf_{n\\to\\infty}n^{4/3}d_n(c)\\ge\\Lambda_c,\n\\]\nwhereas \\(\\mathrm{thm:universal\\text{-}lower}\\) gives\n\\[\n\\limsup_{n\\to\\infty}n^{4/3}d_n(c)\\le\\Lambda_c.\n\\]\nThe two limits therefore coincide.  Substituting the definitions of \\(d_n(c)\\), \\(\\Lambda_c\\), and \\(\\kappa(c)\\) yields\n\\[\nR_n^{\\{0,1\\}}(c)=R_n(c)\n=n^{-1}-\\Lambda_cn^{-4/3}+o(n^{-4/3})\n=n^{-1}-C_AV_c(s_c/2)^{2/3}n^{-4/3}+o(n^{-4/3}).\n\\]\nThe upper theorem proves attainment by the product allocation \\(q_a^\\star=|c_a|/2\\) on active arms and the total nonlinear estimator \\(\\delta_n^\\star\\).  If \\(|S_c|=2\\), \\(\\mathrm{prop:two\\text{-}arm\\text{-}reduction}\\) proves that the two active coefficients are \\(+1\\) and \\(-1\\), that \\(V_c(s_c/2)=1\\), and that inactive labels do not affect either the active-only upper construction or the all-count lower bound.  If \\(|S_c|\\ge3\\), the established response-alphabet upper argument and full-dimensional all-count lower argument give the new closure.  Finally, zero sum and nonzero \\(\\ell^1\\)-norm imply \\(|S_c|\\ge2\\), so these cases exhaust \\(\\mathcal C_K\\).",
    "justification": "The binary equality gives the universal Airy coefficient for every fixed zero-sum, \\(\\ell^1\\)-normalized contrast and is the kernel transported by the bounded reduction.",
    "gap": "The published theorem supplies the support-two base case; no cited source gives the support-at-least-three response-alphabet coefficient or unrestricted all-face lower bound.",
    "consumer": "For an ACTG-175-style four-regimen trial, it determines the second-order allocation and nonlinear shrinkage rule on the binary scale and feeds the bounded-outcome corollary.",
